From a0cd07acdf2ba941834c842752da036e6e57b41b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:50:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] fix(issues): stop issue_write field updates reverting
 concurrent changes

updateIssue read every issue field value over GraphQL, merged in the
requested change and sent the whole set in the issue PATCH. The PATCH
replaces the full set and nothing checked the snapshot was current, so
two overlapping updates to different fields reverted each other: the
call that finished last wrote back the other field's old value.
Deleting one of several fields had the same problem.

Send only the requested values to the additive
POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{issue_number}/issue-field-values
endpoint after the PATCH, and always clear fields through the existing
per-field DELETE, treating 404 as already cleared so a repeated delete
stays a no-op. The PATCH no longer carries issue_field_values, which
also drops the extra GraphQL read and its 25-value cap on this path.
Updates without issue fields are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
